    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Why does Graph Neural Network deserve its own place in the history of artificial intelligence?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Graph neural networks generalized neural computation to data with nodes, edges, and relations. By repeatedly passing messages over a graph, they learned representations for nodes, edges, or whole structures.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-new-model-for-learning-in-graph-domains", "source-unisi-oai-2005-gnn-record"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Each node gathers messages from its neighbors, updates its hidden state, and shares the new state in the next round.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-new-model-for-learning-in-graph-domains"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Experts generally treat GNNs as the foundational deep-learning framework for relational data. Its long-term legacy is message passing, now used in chemistry, recommender systems, knowledge graphs, and scientific modeling.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-the-graph-neural-network-model", "source-a-new-model-for-learning-in-graph-domains"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "As today's systems grow larger, which lessons from Graph Neural Network still matter, and which limits deserve to be questioned again?",
            "sourceIds": [
                "source-the-graph-neural-network-model",
                "source-a-new-model-for-learning-in-graph-domains",
